  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Assume&nbsp;a similar cuboid on top of the given cuboid to make symmetry about charge. Thus, it becomes a cube of length&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>L</mi></math>.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/d0bba6f4-4d57-44cb-b885-79883802a05d-9894750.png\" style=\"width: 350px; height: 262px;\" /></p><p>Flux&nbsp;passing through whole cube is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#981;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>q</mi><msub><mo>&#8712;</mo><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac></math>(Gauss&#39;s Law).</p><p>Since, total faces are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn></math>, so flux&nbsp;passing through shaded face&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>q</mi><mrow><mn>6</mn><msub><mo>&#8712;</mo><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></math>.</p>",
